              "id": "GHSA-xxjr-mmjv-4gpg",
              "shortDescription": {
                 "text": "medium severity - GHSA-xxjr-mmjv-4gpg Improperly Controlled Modification of Object Prototype Attributes ('Prototype Pollution') vulnerability in pkg:npm\/lodash@4.17.15"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "### Impact\n\nThe `_.unset`, `_.omit`, and `_.pullAt` functions are vulnerable to prototype pollution. An attacker can pass crafted paths which cause Lodash to delete methods from global prototypes.\n\nThe issue permits deletion of properties but does not allow overwriting their original behavior.\n\n### Patches\n\nThe issue is patched from 4.17.23 to 4.18.0 depending on the package: `lodash`, `lodash-es`, and `lodash-amd` in 4.17.23, and the standalone `lodash.unset` and `lodash.omit` packages in 4.18.0.\n\n### Workarounds\n\nNone. Upgrade to the patched version."
              },
              "help": {
